From f36f274f6797380bca90c7d76557d5632e48c164 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEMO Phase II executor <executor@nemo.local>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 01:09:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Phase II Rung 2: ice initial-condition machinery
 (area-weighted + override + guard)

Places surface ice on the grid before transport. A user gives ONE total per ice
species under the base name in abundances.in (e.g. "JCO = 1e-4"); read_abundances
defers such base-ice names (coagulation on, per-bin form J01<base> present) instead
of erroring, and dust_ice_place distributes the total across J01<base>..J0N<base>:

  * DEFAULT area-weighted:  X_k = X_total * n_k a_k^2 / sum_j n_j a_j^2, i.e. ice
    coats surface, giving ~uniform initial monolayer coverage; near-empty bins get
    negligible ice by construction.
  * OVERRIDE (surface_ice_distribution.in): "<base> f1..fN" replaces the WHERE for
    that species only (fractions; the total still comes from abundances.in).
    Non-listed species stay area-weighted; fractions not summing to 1 are renormalised
    with a warning.
  * COVERAGE GUARD (override path only): theta_k = X_k/(n_k * nb_sites_per_grain(k));
    warns above COAG_ICE_COVERAGE_WARN monolayers (gross implausibility) but does NOT
    cap -- 2-phase allows multilayers. nb_sites_per_grain is grid-sourced, so the
    guard needs nothing beyond the grid. The default path cannot trigger it.

Gate (d), tests/coag_ice_ic.{f90,sh}, checked at the init state (exact grain IC):
  * round-trip sum_k X_k = X_total                         -> 1.4e-16
  * SHAPE X_k/(n_k a_k^2) constant across bins (proves the area-weighting, not just
    the total)                                             -> spread 1.7e-16
  * coverage negative control: override dumping CO on a near-empty top bin WARNS;
    the area-weighted default on the same grid is SILENT.

Fixture now gives the base total (JCO = 1e-4) exercising the machinery. All prior
Rung 2 gates unchanged: ice conservation 1.4e-15, dust-mass 3.8e-13, ice rate 3.0e-6,
eps split hand-check PASS, jac-on-ice 0 bugs. coag-OFF byte-identical (the deferral
only fires when coagulation is on and the base-ice per-bin form exists).
